      "raw": "## Capillary Documentation MCP Server Setup",
      "kind": "heading",
      "syntax": "markdown",
      "depth": 2,
      "text": "Capillary Documentation MCP Server Setup",
      "target": {
        "component": null,
        "status": "direct"
      },
      "inline": []
    },
    {
      "i": 7,
      "lines": [
        22,
        22
      ],
      "raw": "Capillary Documentation hosts a remote MCP server at `https://docs.capillarytech.com/mcp`. Configure your AI development tools to connect to this server. If your APIs require authentication, you can pass in headers via query parameters or however headers are configured in your MCP client.",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "syntax": "markdown",
      "text": "Capillary Documentation hosts a remote MCP server at https://docs.capillarytech.com/mcp. Configure your AI development tools to connect to this server. If your APIs require authentication, you can pass in headers via query parameters or however headers are configured in your MCP client.",
      "target": {
        "component": null,
        "status": "direct"
      },
      "inline": []
    },
    {
      "i": 8,
      "lines": [
        24,
        67
      ],
      "raw": "<Tabs>\n  <Tab title=\"Cursor\">\n    **Add to `~/.cursor/mcp.json`:**\n\n    ```json\n    {\n      \"mcpServers\": {\n        \"capillary-documentation\": {\n          \"url\": \"https://docs.capillarytech.com/mcp\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n    ```\n\n    </Tab>\n  <Tab title=\"Windsurf\">\n    **Add to `~/.codeium/windsurf/mcp_config.json`:**\n\n    ```json\n    {\n      \"mcpServers\": {\n        \"capillary-documentation\": {\n          \"url\": \"https://docs.capillarytech.com/mcp\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n    ```\n\n  </Tab>\n  <Tab title=\"Claude Desktop\">\n    **Add to `claude_desktop_config.json`:**\n\n    ```json\n    {\n      \"mcpServers\": {\n        \"capillary-documentation\": {\n          \"url\": \"https://docs.capillarytech.com/mcp\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n    ```\n\n  </Tab>\n</Tabs>",
